  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon WASH MHM facilities 2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Name of project: Making emergency WASH facilities inclusive and MHM-friendly: Developing and piloting rapid tools and adaptable designs for MHM and disability-friendly latrines, bathing and laundering areas.
PROJECT SUMMARY: Making emergency WASH facilities accessible and inclusive with development and piloting of rapid community engagement tools and adaptable designs for MHM and disability-friendly latrines, bathing/laundering areas. With an emphasis on respecting dignity while ensuring access, participation and safety.
&#xa0;
Confirmed partners are British Red Cross (BRC) and Arup. Close collaboration with Red Cross Red Crescent (RCRC) Movement partners, as well as local and international organizations working in WASH, shelter, disability and protection in humanitarian contexts, is planned.&#xa0;
Cross-project sharing and learning will be facilitated by the IFRC global WASH team between other HIF-funded RCRC projects in different regions (e.g. Asia, Africa, Middle East).</narrative>
  </description>
